  "label": "white kids are mapped onto the distressed person",
  "description": "The text 'white kids be like \"i have had enough\"' explicitly maps the social group 'white kids' onto the visual entity 'person' who is depicted in a state of emotional overwhelm. The person's distressed expression and body language (covering face, tear-streaked eye) are used as a visual metaphor to represent the supposed emotional state of 'white kids' as described in the text. This is an analogical mapping where the textual entity 'white kids' is projected onto the visual entity 'person' to convey a stereotype or commentary about that group.",
